    "en": {
      "title": "We Used Codex Pro $100 for 30 Days: 14 Resets, $3,221",
      "titleCore": "We Used Codex Pro $100 for 30 Days: 14 Early Resets and $3,221 of API Value",
      "description": "Real logs from a month on Codex Pro $100: 15 weekly windows, 14 early resets, 268,978 requests and $3,221 at API list prices. Charts, tables and method.",
      "body": "<p>In October we ran OpenAI's Codex on the Pro $100 plan and logged every request. The weekly limit refreshed early 14 times in 30 days, giving 15 weekly windows instead of the usual four or five. The usage was worth $3,221 at API list prices, about 32 times the $100 plan price.</p>\n<div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:22px 0'><div style='background:#101726;border:1px solid #1E2A3F;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;flex:1 1 150px'><div style='font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:#E6EAF2;line-height:1.1'>14</div><div style='font-size:13px;color:#7F8BA0;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4'>early resets in 30 days</div></div><div style='background:#101726;border:1px solid #1E2A3F;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;flex:1 1 150px'><div style='font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:#E6EAF2;line-height:1.1'>15</div><div style='font-size:13px;color:#7F8BA0;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4'>weekly windows (a normal month has 4 or 5)</div></div><div style='background:#101726;border:1px solid #1E2A3F;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;flex:1 1 150px'><div style='font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:#E6EAF2;line-height:1.1'>$3,221</div><div style='font-size:13px;color:#7F8BA0;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4'>API-list-price value of the usage</div></div><div style='background:#101726;border:1px solid #1E2A3F;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px;flex:1 1 150px'><div style='font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:#E6EAF2;line-height:1.1'>97.9%</div><div style='font-size:13px;color:#7F8BA0;margin-top:4px;line-height:1.4'>of input tokens came from cache</div></div></div>\n<p style='color:#6B7689;font-size:14px;margin-top:-6px'>Published 3 November 2026 · data 1 to 31 October 2026 (UTC) · method and caveats below</p>\n<p>This is the month-long follow-up to <a href='/research/codex-pro-100-heavy-user-resets-log'>our 12-day Codex log</a>. Same method, same machine, now over 268,978 requests from 2,847 session files, 1 to 31 October 2026 (UTC). The figures are list-price equivalents, not what OpenAI charged, and we say below exactly what they leave out.</p>\n<h2>What surprised us</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>A reset about every two days.</strong> 15 windows in a month where the calendar gives you 4.3. The median window lasted 31 hours, not seven days.</li>\n<li><strong>Resets followed burn-outs.</strong> 9 of the 14 early resets came right after a window that had reached 95% or more. The logs cannot say whether each was an OpenAI-wide reset or a banked reset we redeemed; they only show the gauge jumping back before its scheduled time.</li>\n<li><strong>Almost everything was cache.</strong> 97.9% of the 37.0 billion input tokens were cached reads, which list at a fraction of the normal input price.</li>\n<li><strong>The cheap model did the volume, the expensive one did the damage.</strong> GPT-6 Astra made 1.1% of requests and 17% of the value. GPT-6 Luna made 59% of requests and 8.5% of the value.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The month, window by window</h2>\n<figure style='margin:28px 0 34px'><svg viewBox='0 0 760 434' width='100%' role='img' aria-labelledby='c1t c1d' style='display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto;font-family:inherit'><title id='c1t'>Codex Pro $100: 15 weekly windows in October 2026</title><desc id='c1d'>Each bar is one weekly window. The dashed line shows how long the window was scheduled to run. A new window opened early 14 times.</desc><line x1='64.0' y1='32' x2='64.0' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='64.0' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 1</text><line x1='133.2' y1='32' x2='133.2' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='133.2' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 5</text><line x1='219.6' y1='32' x2='219.6' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='219.6' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 10</text><line x1='306.1' y1='32' x2='306.1' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='306.1' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 15</text><line x1='392.5' y1='32' x2='392.5' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='392.5' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 20</text><line x1='479.0' y1='32' x2='479.0' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='479.0' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 25</text><line x1='582.7' y1='32' x2='582.7' y2='404' stroke='#1E2A3F' stroke-width='1'/><text x='582.7' y='420' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>Oct 31</text><text x='56' y='52' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='end'>W1</text><line x1='87.6' y1='48' x2='167.9' y2='48' stroke='#3B4A66' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='3 3'/><rect x='70.9' y='42' width='16.7' height='12' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='752' y='52' font-size='11' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='end'>$81 · 100%</text><text x='56' y='76' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='end'>W2</text><line x1='96.6' y1='72' x2='208.7' y2='72' stroke='#3B4A66' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='3 3'/><rect x='87.6' y='66' width='8.9' height='12' rx='3' fill='#44608f'/><circle cx='87.6' cy='72' r='3.5' fill='#F5A524' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='752' y='76' font-size='11' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='end'>$35 · 14%</text><text x='56' y='100' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='end'>W3</text><line x1='164.1' y1='96' x2='217.6' y2='96' stroke='#3B4A66' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='3 3'/><rect x='96.6' y='90' width='67.6' height='12' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><circle cx='96.6' cy='96' r='3.5' fill='#F5A524' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='1.5'/><text x='752' y='100' font-size='11' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='end'>$182 · 98%</text><text x='56' y='124' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='end'>W4</text><line x1='184.5' y1='120' x2='293.1' y2='120' stroke='#3B4A66' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='3 3'/><rect x='172.1' y='114' width='12.5' height='12' rx=