e'>W4</text><rect x='243.6' y='154.6' width='32' height='131.4' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='259.6' y='149.6' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$227</text><text x='259.6' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W5</text><rect x='289.7' y='156.6' width='32' height='129.4' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='305.7' y='151.6' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$224</text><text x='305.7' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W6</text><rect x='335.9' y='187.6' width='32' height='98.4' rx='3' fill='#44608f'/><text x='351.9' y='182.6' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$170</text><text x='351.9' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W7</text><rect x='382.0' y='179.7' width='32' height='106.3' rx='3' fill='#44608f'/><text x='398.0' y='174.7' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$184</text><text x='398.0' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W8</text><rect x='428.1' y='151.3' width='32' height='134.7' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='444.1' y='146.3' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$233</text><text x='444.1' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W9</text><rect x='474.3' y='143.9' width='32' height='142.1' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='490.3' y='138.9' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$246</text><text x='490.3' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W10</text><rect x='520.4' y='139.7' width='32' height='146.3' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='536.4' y='134.7' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$253</text><text x='536.4' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W11</text><rect x='566.5' y='191.0' width='32' height='95.0' rx='3' fill='#44608f'/><text x='582.5' y='186.0' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$164</text><text x='582.5' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W12</text><rect x='612.7' y='131.1' width='32' height='154.9' rx='3' fill='#44608f'/><text x='628.7' y='126.1' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$268</text><text x='628.7' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W13</text><rect x='658.8' y='117.3' width='32' height='168.7' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='674.8' y='112.3' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$292</text><text x='674.8' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W14</text><rect x='704.9' y='41.4' width='32' height='244.6' rx='3' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='720.9' y='36.4' font-size='10.5' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='middle' stroke='#0A0F1A' stroke-width='3' paint-order='stroke'>$423</text><text x='720.9' y='302' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0' text-anchor='middle'>W15</text><line x1='52' y1='228.2' x2='744' y2='228.2' stroke='#F5A524' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='2 4'/><text x='58' y='222.2' font-size='11' fill='#F5A524'>$100 plan price</text><line x1='52' y1='137.2' x2='744' y2='137.2' stroke='#4ADE80' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-dasharray='6 4'/><text x='58' y='131.2' font-size='11' fill='#4ADE80'>average fully used window $258</text><text x='52' y='324' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>Bright bars: window reached 95% or more. Dim bars: reset or stopped earlier.</text></svg><figcaption style='color:#7F8BA0;font-size:13px;margin-top:8px;line-height:1.5'>API-list-price value of each window. The 9 windows that were fully used ranged from $182 to $423; the average was $258. Every window except W1 (partial) and W2 was worth more than the plan's full monthly price at list rates.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A fully used window was worth $258 on average, but the spread is wide ($182 to $423). The biggest, window 15, ran for 70 hours and 39,755 requests. Value per percent of gauge is not constant, because it depends on the model mix and how much of the context was cached.</p>\n<h3>Why this is higher than our earlier $175 median</h3>\n<p>Our <a href='/research/chatgpt-pro-100-real-codex-multiplier'>earlier multiplier article</a> measured $100 to $234 per full window, median $175, over six windows between 27 September and 8 October. This month's 9 fully used windows ran $182 to $423, with a median of $237 and a mean of $258. It is the same method on different weeks and a different model mix, so the two sets are not directly comparable. We have not isolated one cause for the difference; the point is that a full window's list-price value is a range, not a fixed number.</p>\n<h2>What would a reset-free month have been?</h2>\n<p>Estimate, not measurement: with one natural window a week, a 31-day month holds 31 / 7 = 4.4 windows. At the average fully used window ($258), that is about $1,141. We measured $3,221, so the early resets made the month worth roughly 2.8 times a no-reset month, or about $2,080 more at list prices. Treat the $1,141 as a rough baseline: our window values varied by more than 2x.</p>\n<h2>Which models used the plan?</h2>\n<figure style='margin:28px 0 34px'><svg viewBox='0 0 760 236' width='100%' role='img' aria-labelledby='c3t c3d' style='display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto;font-family:inherit'><title id='c3t'>Share of requests versus share of API value by model</title><desc id='c3d'>GPT-6 Luna made most requests but little of the value; GPT-6 Astra made about one percent of requests and about seventeen percent of the value.</desc><text x='100' y='66' font-size='12' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='end'>Requests</text><rect x='110.0' y='44' width='209.7' height='34' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='214.8' y='65' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>33%</text><rect x='319.7' y='44' width='7.3' height='34' fill='#C084FC'/><rect x='327.0' y='44' width='377.2' height='34' fill='#4ADE80'/><text x='515.6' y='65' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>59%</text><rect x='704.2' y='44' width='38.1' height='34' fill='#F5A524'/><text x='723.3' y='65' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>6%</text><rect x='742.3' y='44' width='6.7' height='34' fill='#38BDF8'/><rect x='749.0' y='44' width='1.0' height='34' fill='#64748B'/><text x='100' y='132' font-size='12' fill='#E6EAF2' text-anchor='end'>API value</text><rect x='110.0' y='110' width='412.3' height='34' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='316.2' y='131' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>64%</text><rect x='522.3' y='110' width='109.2' height='34' fill='#C084FC'/><text x='576.9' y='131' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>17%</text><rect x='631.5' y='110' width='54.4' height='34' fill='#4ADE80'/><text x='658.7' y='131' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>8%</text><rect x='685.9' y='110' width='44.1' height='34' fill='#F5A524'/><text x='707.9' y='131' font-size='11.5' fill='#0A0F1A' text-anchor='middle' font-weight='600'>7%</text><rect x='730.0' y='110' width='20.0' height='34' fill='#38BDF8'/><rect x='110' y='184' width='10' height='10' rx='2' fill='#7AAFFF'/><text x='125' y='193' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>GPT-6.1 Sol</text><rect x='207.2' y='184' width='10' height='10' rx='2' fill='#C084FC'/><text x='222.2' y='193' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>GPT-6 Astra</text><rect x='304.4' y='184' width='10' height='10' rx='2' fill='#4ADE80'/><text x='319.4' y='193' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>GPT-6 Luna</text><rect x='395.4' y='184' width='10' height='10' rx='2' fill='#F5A524'/><text x='410.4' y='193' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>GPT-6.1 Terra</text><rect x='505.0' y='184' width='10' height='10' rx='2' fill='#38BDF8'/><text x='520.0' y='193' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>GPT-6 Sol</text><rect x='589.8' y='184' width='10' height='10' rx='2' fill='#64748B'/><text x='604.8' y='193' font-size='11' fill='#7F8BA0'>Auto-review (unpriced)</text></svg><figcaption style='color:#7F8BA0;font-size:13px;margin-top:8px;line-height:1.5'>Share of requests (top) versus share of API-list value (bottom) by model. Unlabelled slivers are under 5%.</figcaption></figure>\n<div class='table-wrap' style='overflow-x:auto'><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Requests</th><th>Share</th><th>API value</th><th>Share of value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GPT-6.1 Sol</td><td>88,131</td><td>32.8%</td><td>$2,075</td><td>64.4%</td></tr><tr><td>GPT-6 Astra</td><td>3,066</td><td>1.1%</td><td>$549</td><td>17.1%</td></tr><tr><td>GPT-6 Luna</td><td>158,539</td><td>58.9%</td><td>$274</td><td>8.5%</td></tr><tr><td>GPT-6.1 Terra</td><td>16,000</td><td>5.9%</td><td>$222</td><td>6.9%</td></tr><tr><td>GPT-6 Sol</td><td>2,817</td><td>1.0%</td><td>$101</td><td>3.1%</td></tr><tr><td>Auto-review (unpriced)</td><td>425</td><td>0.2%</td><td>unpriced</td><td>-</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>GPT-6.1 Sol carried 64% of the value. The lesson is the same one we see in API bills: request counts say little about spend. Count value by model, not requests. See <a href='/research/cost-per-successful-task'>cost per successful task</a> for the measure that matters once you add retries.</p>\n<h2>How we measured it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Source:</strong> Codex's local session logs. Each request records cumulative token counts and the rate-limit state (plan type, weekly percent used, scheduled reset time). The plan type read <code>prolite</code> throughout, which is Pro $100 (see the <a href='/research/codex-pro-100-heavy-user-resets-log'>earlier log</a>).</li>\n<li><strong>Value:</strong> each request's token change priced at OpenAI's published short-context rates (inputs up to 272K tokens) from the <a href='https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing'>OpenAI pricing page</a>, checked 3 November 2026: GPT-6.1 Sol $2.00 input, $0.10 cached, $10.00 output per million tokens; GPT-6 Astra $10 / $1 / $50; GPT-6 Luna $0.10 / $0.01 / $0.50; GPT-6.1 Terra $1 / $0.05 / $5; GPT-6 Sol $2 / $0.20 / $10.</li>\n<li><strong>Windows:</strong> a new window starts when the scheduled reset time changes. Mixed sessions sometimes report stale reset times, which produced 35 raw fragments; we merged fragments that shared a reset time into the 15 real windows above. An early reset is a window that opened more than five minutes before the previous one was scheduled to end.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>What the numbers leave out</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>425 auto-review requests (0.16% of the total) use a model with no published price and are counted as $0.</li>\n<li>Requests over 272K input tokens would price higher than the short-context rates used here.</li>\n<li>326 log lines could not be parsed, and the logs end on 31 October at 05:56 UTC.</li>\n<li>List-price value is a way to size usage. It is not an invoice, a saving, or a promise that later months will match; OpenAI sets plan limits and can change them.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What to take from it</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Measure per window, not per month.</strong> A monthly average hid windows from $182 to $423.</li>\n<li><strong>Log the gauge and the reset time with every request.</strong> It is the only way to see an early reset after the fact.</li>\n<li><strong>Watch cache share and model mix.</strong> They moved the value more than request counts did. For the mechanics, see <a href='/research/codex-prompt-caching-cost'>Codex prompt caching cost</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Plan the reset, do not count on it.</strong> Read <a href='/research/codex-banked-reset-when-to-redeem'>when to redeem a banked reset</a> and the <a href='/research/codex-reset-history'>dated reset history</a> before you build a workflow around one.</li>\n</ol>\n",
